  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through Saturday)\nIssued at 1007 PM CDT Sat Oct 3 2026\n\nSurface high pressure by the mid week should be situated over the\ncoastal Mid Atlantic region. An anticyclonic flow rounding the \nwestern periphery of this high will bring a SE flow across the \nDeep South, and help continue a gradual warming trend. Despite the\ndays getting shorter progressing trough the autumn, above normal \nwarmth should continue for the mid and latter portions of the new \nweek. Highs on Wed should rise into the low/mid 80s under \ngenerally sunny skies. Temperatures should creep up a tad both Thu\nand Fri, with highs on Fri in the mid/upper 80s. Lows Wed and Thu\nnight should range from the mid/upper 40s in those normally \ncooler locations, to the mid 50s near large bodies of water. \nNormal high/low temperatures by Fri, Oct 9th are around 79/55.\n\nThe SE flow will gradually bring more moisture and clouds inland \nfrom the Gulf region was we near the weekend. Enough of this \nmoisture return will also bring lower end rain chances back to the\nTennessee Valley - right in time for the next upcoming weekend. \nThe moisture should make for somewhat milder conditions Fri night \nwith lows in the 50s, and highs on Sat with rain chances in the \nlow/mid 80s.",
